COMPILATION: 
    gcc main.c -o bots -lpthread

EXECUTION:
    ./bots

CLEANUP:
    make clean

Design Decisions:
    Numbered ids were assigned and passed to each thread which made it safe to determine which threads where odd and even.
    Each thread was given a sleep behavior depening on its odd or even status so threads wait periodically. The semaphore 
    FLAG was used to ensure thread remained exclusive when accessing the share file, which prevents data corruption. pthread_join()
    is called in a seperate loop after all threads are created to ensure all 7 threads run concurrently. 

Extra feautres:
    Each line in the QUOTE.txt file is numbered. The code keeps track how many lines have been created in the txt file.

Deficiencies:
    I had a hard time understanding the instructions, specfically the part in which id (pthread_id() or an int) was suppose to show with the thread.

Lessons Learned:
    We learned how to use semaphores to prevent conditions where multiple threads access a shared resource. We also learned how synchorinization processes
    are essential for maintaining data intact in multi-thread programs. 